\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  VIEW:Yen Gains Prompt Watch For Signs Of  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 644 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 September 2010\par 22:24\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds Internet link to trendline.)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Karen Johnson \par    A DOW JONES NEWSWIRES COLUMN \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 The dollar fell Thursday to its lowest level in more than a week versus the yen, leaving traders on watch for signs of fresh Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 With no apparent official buying of U.S. dollars and selling to hinder yen appreciation, investors wondered what it would take for the Japanese to authorize another round of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Adam Cole\uc2 , head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\uc2  in London, said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again. The question is when.\par \par \uc2 "I think it's dictated by the level rather than the timing ... and I think we're pretty close to the danger zone at the moment," Cole said.\par \par \uc2 Others said Japan was delaying its next move until after Thursday's meeting between U.S. President Barack Obama and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  Prime Minister Naoto Kan. \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to be a topic of discussion at those talks.\par \par \uc2 Last week, the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  entered the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the first time in six years, selling Y2 trillion and buying up U.S. dollars in a bid to weaken the rising yen. Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda said Friday \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again if necessary to weaken the yen.\par \par \uc2 "Domestically, politically, they can't really be perceived to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  once and then immediately admit defeat," Cole said. He believed Japan is closely watching a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  "zone," between Y83.00 and Y85.00.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the dollar hit a post-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  low at Y84.26 in New York, and held close to that level for the remainder of the day.\par \par \uc2 Carl Forcheski, director of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2  in New York, said he is watching the downward trendline extending from May to the top of the post-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  push just a few days ago.\par \par \uc2 To view the trendline, please see:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://dowjoneswebservices.com/chart/view/4626"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://dowjoneswebservices.com/chart/view/4626}}}\par \par \uc2 If the dollar breaks above that line it could shoot higher, as the move would trigger automatic orders to buy it against the yen.\par \par \uc2 The stop loss orders, "which likely lie just above that trendline and the 86.00 level, may give the dollar and the [Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 ] more 'bang for the buck', " Forcheski said, reducing the drive for official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 As \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's intent is likely to curb further yen appreciation rather than push the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  significantly lower, further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be relatively contained by data as well, said Hidetoshi Yanagihara, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Mizuho Corporate Bank\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 Improvement in U.S. economic data toward the end of the year could bolster the dollar and reduce the need for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But the recovery remains uncertain, and if the U.S. economy continues to struggle, the yen could benefit from safe-haven flows, increasing the need for further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he added.\par \par \uc2 With \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's markets closed for Autumn Equinox Day, and markets in China, Hong Kong and South Korea also on holidays, major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday were trading in narrow ranges.\par \par \uc2 "Right now there is a lot more talk and innuendo and wondering going on than there seems to be actual \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2 's Forcheski.\par \par \uc2 (Karen Johnson writes about Canadian fixed income and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets for Dow Jones Newswires. She can be reached at 416-306-2022; or via email: karen.johnson@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 (Don Curren in Toronto contributed to this article.)\par \par \uc2 (TALK BACK: We invite readers to send us comments on this or other financial news topics. Please email us at TalkbackAmericas@dowjones.com. Readers should include their full names, work or home addresses and telephone numbers for verification purposes. We reserve the right to edit and publish your comments along with your name; we reserve the right not to publish reader comments.) [ 09-23-10 1624ET ]\par \par \uc2 1141   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100923e69n000bk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
