ibility of a short-term correction given overbought studies. The next key resistance level comes in at 0.9850, support at 0.9433." Last 0.9556, hit 0.9595 offshore. (enda.curran@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 2147 GMT [Dow Jones] \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's MOF may delay any further plans for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to strengthen USD/JPY due to scheduled meeting between PM Kan and U.S. President Obama, says RBC \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Strategist Matthew Strauss. USD/JPY last 84.525, traded to 84.28 overnight, the lowest level since MOF \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week at 83.00. "The depreciation of almost 1.5% during the last two trading days must sit uncomfortably with the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , increasing the risk of further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." (enda.curran@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 2121 GMT [Dow Jones] EUR/USD likely to keep gaining in Asia; "It is currently the classic anti-dollar instrument. It's got momentum on its side. It is getting a bit over bought but it still has a lot of momentum behind it," says \uc2 Westpac\b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Strategist Imre Speizer. Pair last 1.3400, tips resistance at 1.3440, support around 1.3330. Says with no reason for it to collapse, may well test resistance on day. (rebecca.howard@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 2120 GMT [Dow Jones] U.S. SUMMARY: USD dipped to lowest level against EUR since April as investors ditched greenback on speculation Fed could soon act to kick-start slowing U.S. economy. USD weakened against JPY to lowest mark since last week's massive Y2 trillion \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dipping below Y84.50 and putting investors on watch for another round of yen-weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Fed's specific mention of weaker-than-targeted inflation has added a weight around USD's already stressed neck, says Sacha Tihanyi, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Scotia Capital in Toronto; "The overarching reason to dislike the dollar has broadened." EUR/USD at 1.3394 late Wednesday vs 1.3247 late Tuesday, USD/JPY at 84.54 vs 85.12, EUR/JPY at 113.22 vs 112.75, GBP/USD at 1.5669 vs 1.5627, USD/CHF at 0.9864 vs 0.9976. USD Index at 79.812 vs 80.442. Stocks slipped as investors worried about Fed's suggestion economy may need additional stimulative measures; \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  fell 2.2% as software company launched bond issue worth at least $4.75 billion. Dow fell 0.2%, Nasdaq fell 0.6%, Philly semicons down 1.4%. Long-dated treasurys rose as speculation continued that Fed will buy bonds at larger scale in coming months; 2-year yields flat at 0.428%, 10-years down 3 bps at 2.546%. December Comex gold rose $17.80 to $1,292.10/oz. November Nymex crude settled 26 cents lower at $74.71/bbl after unexpected increase in U.S. stockpiles of oil, fuel products. (rebecca.howard@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 2102 GMT [Dow Jones] NZ government bonds, IRS unchanged early in NZ with market largely treading ahead of 2Q GDP data, also government bond tender later in session. Local bond trader says tender likely to go well given reasonable demand; Debt Management Office planning to sell NZ$450 million including NZ$250 million of April 2015s. "I think the market will be fairly quiet until we get GDP out of the way and then it will be gearing up for the tender." 2-year swap rates unchanged at 3.785%, 10-years unchanged at 4.94%, November 2011 bond yields unchanged at 3.605%. (rebecca.howard@dowjones.com) [ 09-22-10 1846ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100922e69m000dz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
