i, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Scotia Capital in Toronto; "The overarching reason to dislike the dollar has broadened." EUR/USD at 1.3394 late Wednesday vs 1.3247 late Tuesday, USD/JPY at 84.54 vs 85.12, EUR/JPY at 113.22 vs 112.75, GBP/USD at 1.5669 vs 1.5627, USD/CHF at 0.9864 vs 0.9976. USD Index at 79.812 vs 80.442. Stocks slipped as investors worried about Fed's suggestion economy may need additional stimulative measures; \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  fell 2.2% as software company launched bond issue worth at least $4.75 billion. Dow fell 0.2%, Nasdaq fell 0.6%, Philly semicons down 1.4%. Long-dated treasurys rose as speculation continued that Fed will buy bonds at larger scale in coming months; 2-year yields flat at 0.428%, 10-years down 3 bps at 2.546%. December Comex gold rose $17.80 to $1,292.10/oz. November Nymex crude settled 26 cents lower at $74.71/bbl after unexpected increase in U.S. stockpiles of oil, fuel products. (rebecca.howard@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 2102 GMT [Dow Jones] NZ government bonds, IRS unchanged early in NZ with market largely treading ahead of 2Q GDP data, also government bond tender later in session. Local bond trader says tender likely to go well given reasonable demand; Debt Management Office planning to sell NZ$450 million including NZ$250 million of April 2015s. "I think the market will be fairly quiet until we get GDP out of the way and then it will be gearing up for the tender." 2-year swap rates unchanged at 3.785%, 10-years unchanged at 4.94%, November 2011 bond yields unchanged at 3.605%. (rebecca.howard@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 4:53 (Dow Jones) If Blockbuster (BLOKA) does file for bankruptcy, as Wednesday's buzz suggests, NCR reiterates its Blockbuster Express DVD kiosks won't be affected. NCR, which licenses the brand from the floundering movie rental chain, notes it doesn't rely on BLOKA for capital to operate the machines. "It is business as usual for NCR," says company spokesman. NCR say