\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK:  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2 's MOF May Delay Fresh  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  - RBC\b0\par\par\uc2 1,317 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 September 2010\par 23:47\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; \par MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2147 GMT [Dow Jones] \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's MOF may delay any further plans for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to strengthen USD/JPY due to scheduled meeting between PM Kan and U.S. President Obama, says RBC \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Strategist Matthew Strauss. USD/JPY last 84.525, traded to 84.28 overnight, the lowest level since MOF \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  last week at 83.00. "The depreciation of almost 1.5% during the last two trading days must sit uncomfortably with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , increasing the risk of further \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ." (enda.curran@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 2121 GMT [Dow Jones] EUR/USD likely to keep gaining in Asia; "It is currently the classic anti-dollar instrument. It's got momentum on its side. It is getting a bit over bought but it still has a lot of momentum behind it," says \uc2 Westpac\b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Strategist Imre Speizer. Pair last 1.3400, tips resistance at 1.3440, support around 1.3330. Says with no reason for it to collapse, may well test resistance on day. (rebecca.howard@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 2120 GMT [Dow Jones] U.S. SUMMARY: USD dipped to lowest level against EUR since April as investors ditched greenback on speculation Fed could soon act to kick-start slowing U.S. economy. USD weakened against JPY to lowest mark since last week's massive Y2 trillion \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dipping below Y84.50 and putting investors on watch for another round of yen-weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Fed's specific mention of weaker-than-targeted inflation has added a weight around USD's already stressed neck, says Sacha Tihanyi, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Scotia Capital in Toronto; "The overarching reason to dislike the dollar has broadened." EUR/USD at 1.3394 late Wednesday vs 1.3247 late Tuesday, USD/JPY at 84.54 vs 85.12, EUR/JPY at 113.22 vs 112.75, GBP/USD at 1.5669 vs 1.5627, USD/CHF at 0.9864 vs 0.9976. USD Index at 79.812 vs 80.442. Stocks slipped as investors worried about Fed's suggestion economy may need additional stimulative measures; \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  fell 2.2% as software company launched bond issue worth at least $4.75 billion. Dow fell 0.2%, Nasdaq fell 0.6%, Philly semicons down 1.4%. Long-dated treasurys rose as speculation continued that Fed will buy bonds at larger scale in coming months; 2-year yields flat at 0.428%, 10-years down 3 bps at 2.546%. December Comex gold rose $17.80 to $1,292.10/oz. November Nymex crude settled 26 cents lower at $74.71/bbl after unexpected increase in U.S. stockpiles of oil, fuel products. (rebecca.howard@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 2102 GMT [Dow Jones] NZ government bonds, IRS unchanged early in NZ with market largely treading ahead of 2Q GDP data, also government bond tender later in session. Local bond trader says tender likely to go well given reasonable demand; Debt Management Office planning to sell NZ$450 million including NZ$250 million of April 2015s. "I think the market will be fairly quiet until we get GDP out of the way and then it will be gearing up for the tender." 2-year swap rates unchanged at 3.785%, 10-years unchanged at 4.94%, November 2011 bond yields unchanged at 3.605%. (rebecca.howard@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 4:53 (Dow Jones) If Blockbuster (BLOKA) does file for bankruptcy, as Wednesday's buzz suggests, NCR reiterates its Blockbuster Express DVD kiosks won't be affected. NCR, which licenses the brand from the floundering movie rental chain, notes it doesn't rely on BLOKA for capital to operate the machines. "It is business as usual for NCR," says company spokesman. NCR says it wrote "legal protections" into licensing pact to ensure continued \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  "for years to come." (melissa.korn@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 Call us at (415) 439-6402 or email andrew.morse@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 Visit the Market Talk website at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.djnmarkettalk.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.djnmarkettalk.com}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 2020 GMT [Dow Jones] NZD/USD dragged higher by broadly weaker USD, breaking through 0.7400 for first time since January overnight; last 0.7381. But both NZ-U.S. 3-year swap spreads, global risk appetite well below levels prevailing when NZD/USD last above 0.7400, says BNZ \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Strategist Mike Jones; "This suggests USD weakness, rather than 'fundamentals' has been the key driver of the recent bout of NZD/USD strength." Says today's 2Q GDP will help determine whether NZD/USD can hold recent gains; GDP likely expanded 0.8% on-quarter, according to median forecast of 13 economists polled by Dow Jones. Says with RBNZ tipping expansion of 0.9% on quarter "we'll have to see a significant upside surprise for markets to ratchet RBNZ OCR expectations higher." (rebecca.howard@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 2012 GMT [Dow Jones] The dollar fell against the euro, which reached its strongest level since April, as investors ditched the greenback on speculation the Federal Reserve could soon act to kickstart a slowing U.S. economy. The dollar weakened against the yen to its lowest mark since last week's massive Y2 trillion \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dipping below Y84.50 and putting investors on watch for another round of yen-weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The ICE Dollar Index, which tracks the greenback against a trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , slumped to its lowest level since March. And the greenback also fell to its lowest level since March 2008 against the Swiss franc.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (andrewj.johnson@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2004 GMT [Dow Jones] In final push, agency mortgage-backeds lagged Treasurys in both directions on Wed, according to Paul Jacob at Banc of Manhattan Capital. Risk premiums are quoted at 145bps/Tsys. "There is rising concern over prepayment risk," he added.(anusha.shrivastava@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1957 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/CAD is ending higher at 1.0298, a moderate advance from its late Tues level of 1.0261 but a sharp rebound from its session low of 1.0191, according to EBS. CAD underperformed broadly after a volatile session where crude oil futures slumped and Canadian retail sales data for July proved disappointing. There are no significant Canadian data releases Thu. (don.curren@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1937 GMT [Dow Jones] Futures contracts on long-end Treasurys settle higher Wednesday as a mild slide in US stocks combines with Fed's muted outlook on inflation to lure more investors into fixed income. Dec 30-yr bond futures settle 21/32 higher at 132-23, putting the expected yield above 3.75% at contract expiration in late December, according to Optima Investment Research. Dec 10-yr note futures settle 6/32 higher, above a 2.5-week high, as yields seen below 2.625% mark. Eurodollar futures flat to slightly lower in listless price action Wednesday, with front-month Dec contract unchanged at 99.635 at mkt's close.(jacob.bunge@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1954 GMT [Dow Jones] NZD/USD made brief overnight excursion into 0.7400 territory overnight, touching 0.7417, but quickly reversed, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 ANZ Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 ; pair last 0.7378 vs 0.7366 late yesterday. Focus now shifting to NZ 2Q GDP, due at 2245 GMT. Tips a range of 0.7305-0.7385; "topside levels will again be capped by willing sellers around 0.7400." (rebecca.howard@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1940 GMT [Dow Jones] It seems that many market players in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  derivatives still like the old school method of performing some of the most complex trades in the pit. During \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  panel discussion, \f28 \uc2 \f2 UBS\f28 \uc2 \f2  managing director Mark Schlater said people still like to pick up the phone and talk to a broker about a position. CME \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  director Craig LeVeille said only six percent of spreads on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  options are performed on the electronic platform. [ 09-22-10 1747ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100922e69m000dn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
