\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 :Dollar Falls Broadly; Fed's Possible Easing Weighs\b0\par\par\uc2 By Andrew J. Johnson and Bradley Davis   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 855 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 September 2010\par 22:18\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--The dollar dropped to its lowest level against the euro since April as investors broadly ditched the greenback Wednesday on speculation the Federal Reserve could soon act to kick-start a slowing U.S. economy.\par \par \uc2 Talk of a fresh round of growth-stimulating asset purchases, known as quantitative easing, weighed heavily on the greenback, which has suffered as people use cheap dollars to fund bets on higher-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The dollar weakened even against the low-yielding yen to its lowest mark since last week's massive Y2 trillion \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dipping below Y84.50 and putting investors on watch for another round of yen-weakening \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The ICE Dollar Index, which tracks the greenback against a trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , slumped to its lowest level since March, while the greenback fell to its lowest level since March 2008 against the Swiss franc.\par \par \uc2 The Fed's specific mention of weaker-than-targeted inflation has added a weight around the dollar's already stressed neck, said Sacha Tihanyi, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Scotia Capital in Toronto.\par \par \uc2 "The overarching reason to dislike the dollar has broadened," he said. "Where recently it was a loss in growth momentum, it now becomes the fear that policy will ease further and not be normalized for some time, along with the recognition that the [Fed] is certainly worried about the prospects for deflation," he said.\par \par \uc2 Late Wednesday, the euro was at $1.3394, up from $1.3247 late Tuesday, according to EBS via CQG. The dollar was at Y84.54 down from Y85.12, while the euro was at Y113.22, up from Y112.75. The U.K. pound was at $1.5669, up from $1.5627. The dollar was at CHF0.9864, down from CHF0.9976.\par \par \uc2 The ICE Dollar Index, which tracks the greenback against a trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dropped by nearly 1%, sinking to 79.812 from 80.442 late Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The fear of more quantitative easing by the Fed has been enough to move the needle on the dollar, even if investors are ultimately wrong on their assumption of a fresh round of stimulus, said Geoffrey Yu, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 UBS\uc2  in London. The verbal posturing by the Fed has done its job, he said. "The Fed is saying something negative on the dollar right now, in an effort to lower it," Yu said.\par \par \uc2 The euro took advantage of the dollar's woes, with the common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gaining nearly 1% as it also benefited from a successful auction of Portuguese government debt.\par \par \uc2 To see the euro's performance against the dollar, please see: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.dowjoneswebservices.com/chart/view/4618"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.dowjoneswebservices.com/chart/view/4618}}}\par \par \uc2 With the dollar also dipping below the Y85 mark, coming off last week's post-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  highs, the threat of a new round of Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  loomed.\par \par \uc2 There were no signs of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market Wednesday, even as investors pushed the dollar lower, said Hidetoshi Yanagihara, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Mizuho Corporate Bank\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 Some yen watchers said the Japanese government might wait to act until a meeting takes place Thursday between President Barack Obama and Japan's Prime Minister Naoto Kan. "Anything less would surely be a finger in the eye of the president," said David Gilmore, a partner at \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Analytics in Essex, Conn.\par \par \uc2 Norway's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  distinguished itself from the Fed after it kept its key interest rate unchanged at 2.0% Wednesday, as expected, but gave a firm signal that it will look to raise borrowing costs in the future. That helped the Norwegian krone ride the wave of antidollar sentiment, with the greenback falling more than 1.2% against the krone.\par \par \uc2 Among other higher-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Brazilian real bucked the trend of strengthening against the dollar after the local Estado news agency reported Wednesday the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Brazil would coordinate purchases of dollars using a government investment fund to help curb gains in the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . That led the higher-yielding real to lose about 0.5% against the greenback.\par \par \uc2 Separately, the Russian ruble weakened to a new seven-month low against a basket of dollars and euros. Once considered a high flier after bouncing 26% off its lows against the dollar in 2009, the ruble is now the worst performing emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the third quarter.\par \par \uc2 With the ICE Dollar Index weakening, \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2 's PowerShares U.S. Dollar Index Bearish exchange-traded fund was up 0.79% from late Tuesday, while its PowerShares U.S. Dollar Index Bullish was down 0.77%. The two exchange-traded funds are based on \uc2 Deutsche Bank\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures indexes, whose composition mirrors that of the ICE's Dollar Index.\par \par \uc2 -By Andrew J. Johnson and Bradley Davis, Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-3092; andrewj.johnson@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (James Glynn in Sydney, Ira Iosebashvili in Moscow and Anthony Esposito in Santiago contributed to this article.) [ 09-22-10 1618ET ]\par \par \uc2 1033 1074 1158 1863 1865 20714 28038 4164   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100922e69m000d4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
