ket analyst at Meiwa Securities. "I doubt the (prior executed) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be a one-off event, but it will be hard to do again immediately after the dollar fell below 85 yen," he adds, noting timing of next prospective \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be difficult. Says markets also closely eyeing talks between PM Kan and U.S. President Obama expected on Thursday. 25/33 Topix subindexes lower, with exporters such as Fanuc (6954.TO) down 0.8% at Y10,500, Canon (7751.TO) down 1.2% at Y3,860. Panasonic (6752.TO) up 3.5% at Y1,150 on Nikkei report it expects to cancel equity financing plan. (kana.inagaki@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0035 GMT [Dow Jones] Thai stocks still remain attractive despite running up 30% since end of anti-government protests mid-May, says Ian Gisbourne, head of Thailand equity research at \uc2 UBS\uc2 ; he tells CNBC that Thailand's fundamentals remain strong with "manufacturing, tourism and agriculture all looking positive." House estimates Thai company earnings to rise 20% next year, but there's potential to revise that upwards. "There's certainly room for earnings to be raised from here and that means the market that, prima facie, looks expensive, isn't really that expensive." Energy, cyclical stocks still underperformers. Also says \uc2 Bank of Thailand\uc2  clearly concerned about THB at 13-year highs vs USD, which should prompt it to leave policy rate unchanged at 1.75% for remainder of 2010 before modest increases in 2011. (leigh.murray@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0034 GMT [Dow Jones] NZ 2Q current account deficit has started to widen as expected, but impact of Canterbury earthquake likely to aid balance in coming quarters, says ASB economist Jane Turner; "We expect the overall impact (of the earthquake) will be to narrow the current account deficit temporarily, due to the one-off transfer coming from the insurance payouts." Says wealth impact of earthquake will manifest in international investment positions as state-owned insurance entity Earthquake Commission may sell some of its holdings of foreign assets, government may have to increase debt issuance to pay for public sector damage. (lucy.craymer@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0019 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/MYR falls to 3.0920 vs 3.1000 late yesterday, fresh 13-year low; pair lower in tandem with USD decline against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Dealers say breach of major 3.1000 support likely to accelerate USD/MYR's fall near-term. "We expect the next immediate support at 3.0750 to be tested soon," dealer says. (benjamin.low@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0011 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/JPY breaks through overnight low marked after FOMC statement, hits fresh intraday low at 84.91, lowest in one week; investors sell pair amid broad USD weakness, in part to test MOF's resolve on any further USD-buying, JPY-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , says Shuichi Kanehira, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at \uc2 Mizuho Corporate Bank\uc2 . Says key technical level at 84.40-84.50 now in sight. Meanwhile, says if MOF does again wade into markets, effectiveness of further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would depend on size of USD-buying, JPY-selling. "\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have to show its resolve" for further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be effective amid broad-based USD weakness. (kosaku.narioka@dowjones.com) [ 09-21-10 2058ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100922e69m0000n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
