\par\par \b \uc2 JGBs rise, prospects for more easing mount after Fed\b0\par\par\uc2 667 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 September 2010\par 02:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Fed meeting feeds expectations of more BOJ easing\par \par \uc2 * December JGB futures hit a 3-wk high, curve flattens\par \par \uc2 * Investors buy superlongs, some eye pocketing profits\par \par \uc2 By Shinichi Saoshiro\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Sept 22 (Reuters) - Japanese government bonds gained on Wednesday as U.S. Treasuries rallied after the Federal Reserve signalled it was open to future easing, which also fed expectations for further policy loosening by the Bank of Japan.\par \par \uc2 The Fed on Tuesday left monetary policy unchanged but opened the door for future easing, saying it stood ready to provide more support for the economy and expressing stronger concerns about low inflation.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's statement came just as expectations for further BOJ easing had been raised after \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the first time in six years last week to knock the yen off a 15-year high against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 "The Fed's stance definitely adds pressure on the BOJ to loosen monetary policy further," said a fund manager at a domestic asset management firm.\par \par \uc2 "The BOJ's recent easing efforts appear to be countermeasures against a strong yen. Shrinking interest rate differentials between Japan and the United States as a result of Fed easing could strengthen the yen and force the BOJ to act again."\par \par \uc2 The spread between U.S. and Japanese five-year government debt yields dipped below 1 percent for the first time in 17 months.\par \par \uc2 The greenback, which has weakened against the yen as the U.S.-Japan interest rate gap has steadily narrowed, fell sharply against the yen following the Fed statement, testing Japan's resolve to keep its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the back foot.\par \par \uc2 Analysts say potential further easing steps include the BOJ expanding its fixed-funding \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  and increasing the amount of JGBs it buys from the market.\par \par \uc2 BOJ board member Ryuzo Miyao said on Wednesday that increasing JGB purchases was an option, but he added that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not have preset ideas about future policy.\par \par \uc2 The BOJ opting not to absorb from the market the yen it sells for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would add to money market liquidity and is also seen as a form of easing.\par \par \uc2 The JGB yield curve flattened on prospects of the BOJ having to commit to a loose monetary stance for a longer period than it may have intended.\par \par \uc2 The 10-year/30-year yield spread tightened by 1 basis point to 86.5 basis points, pulling away from a six-month peak of 91 basis points hit last week.\par \par \uc2 December 10-year JGB futures rose 0.27 point to 142.65 after hitting a three-week high of 142.77.\par \par \uc2 "Some technical indications may suggest that futures are overbought, but sellers have been relatively subdued so far as market sentiment supports further gains," said a dealer at a foreign brokerage.\par \par \uc2 Technical signals were bullish, with futures rising above the cloud, as well as the tenkan and kijun lines, on the Ichimoku chart, which is popular with Japanese traders.\par \par \uc2 Longer-dated cash JGBs were supported as a variety of domestic banks joined traditional buyers such as life insurers to buy superlongs, market players said.\par \par \uc2 "Many of the superlong buyers appear to be buying to pocket profits should the maturities rise further in price in the near future," the fund manager at the domestic asset management firm said.\par \par \uc2 The 30-year yield dropped 3 basis points to 1.890 percent. The yield fell to a seven-year low of 1.535 percent late in August before surging to 2.065 percent last week.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark 10-year yield fell 2 basis points to 1.025 percent and the five-year yield edged down 1 basis point to 0.280 percent.\par \par \uc2 U.S. Treasury prices surged after the Fed's statement, with the yield on the two-year note hitting a series of record lows. (Editing by Joseph Radford)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-JAPAN-JGB (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABX|BNX|FUN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100925e69m0000d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
