\par\par \b \uc2 FACTBOX-Steps countries are taking to counter hot money\b0\par\par\uc2 500 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 September 2010\par 22:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 Sept 22 (Reuters) - More governments around the world are moving to keep their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  from appreciating as investors, turning their backs on low interest rates in developed economies, pour money into higher-yielding markets.\par \par \uc2 The following are recent cases of direct or indirect government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, compiled by Reuters:\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 JAPAN INTERVENES\b0 \highlight\uc2  FOR FIRST TIME SINCE 2004\par \par \uc2 * Prime minister signals Tokyo ready to keep \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Kan to explain to Obama motives for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Yen fell 3 pct on first day of gov't yen selling\par \par \uc2 For related stories, see [ID:nSGE68G0I8]\par \par \uc2 BRAZIL TAKES MORE AGGRESSIVE ACTION\par \par \uc2 * Brazil authorizes sovereign wealth fund to buy dollars\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  steps up daily dollar auctions\par \par \uc2 * Government dismisses chatter of capital controls\par \par \uc2 For related stories, see [ID:nN20102448] [ID:nN23213114]\par \par \uc2 SWITZERLAND HOLDS OFF ON \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Cenbank spent nearly 200 bln Sfr via \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  from March 2009\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  stopped in June of this year\par \par \uc2 * Traders speculate \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  move could prompt SNB to resume \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Swiss franc flirting with parity against dollar\par \par \uc2 For related stories, see [ID:nLDE68D1IK]\par \par \uc2 CHILE WARNS ON PESO, NO \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  YET\par \par \uc2 * Chile \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  ups rate 50 bps, eyes on peso\par \par \uc2 * Peso trading around same level that triggered \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2008\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  issues threats but reluctant to act\par \par \uc2 For related stories, see [ID:nN16244652]\par \par \uc2 SOUTH KOREA SPOTTED BUYING DOLLARS\par \par \uc2 * Spotted buying small amount of dollars - dealers\par \par \uc2 * Move seen as aimed at keeping won below 1,160 per dollar\par \par \uc2 * Government frequently seen buying dollars this year\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves post biggest monthly gain in 14 months\par \par \uc2 For related stories, see [ID:nTOE66R00T]\par \par \uc2 INDONESIA \b \highlight22\uc2 CENTRAL BANK\b0 \highlight\uc2  WIDENS RANGE OF MATURITIES\par \par \uc2 * Cenbank introduced a minimum holding period for its bills in June\par \par \uc2 * Cenbank offered a wider range of maturities\par \par \uc2 * Investors must now hold the bills for minimum of one month\par \par \uc2 For related stories, see [ID:nSGE65F0BV] [ID:nJAK210755]\par \par \uc2 COLOMBIA \b \highlight22\uc2 CENTRAL BANK\b0 \highlight\uc2  BUYS DOLLARS\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  starts buying at least $20 million daily\par \par \uc2 * Analysts say move insufficient, other measures expected\par \par \uc2 * Accumulation of reserves to last at least four months\par \par \uc2 For related stories, see [ID:nN20274631] [ID:nN15183902] [ID:nN15145483]\par \par \uc2 PERU EASES GRIP ON FUND OUTFLOWS\par \par \uc2 * Pension funds allowed to hold more assets abroad\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading near two-year high against dollar\par \par \uc2 * Peru's sol to be boosted by 6-7 pct growth in 2011\par \par \uc2 For related stories, see [ID:nN14108242]\par \par \uc2 ROMANIA \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  CITED AS LEU FIRMS\par \par \uc2 * Cenbank has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly since late 2008\par \par \uc2 For related stories, see [ID:nLDE68D0W7]\par \par \uc2 THAILAND TRYING TO SLOW BAHT GAINS\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says no plans for new tools to curb inflows\par \par \uc2 * Could announce measures to encourage outflows\par \par \uc2 * Baht one of Asia's best-performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year\par \par \uc2 For related stories, see [ID:nSGE68K083] (For a TAKE A LOOK on global money flows and investment strategy, please double-click [ID:nINVEST] (For more details on Asia capital controls, please double-click [ID:TOE68F05F]\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2 -GLOBAL/ (FACTBOX, UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|E|RBN|U|D|M|Z|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100922e69m001bn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
