\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ ADB's Kuroda: Yen Was Overvalued Ahead Of  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2 's  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 487 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 September 2010\par 19:32\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2010, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 21 Sep 2010 13:32 EDT *DJ  ADB's Kuroda: US, Europe, Japan Unlikely To Return To Recession\par \par \uc2 21 Sep 2010 13:33 EDT =DJ  ADB's Kuroda: Yen Was Overvalued Ahead Of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Michael S. Derby \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--A former top Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  official on Tuesday said the yen was overvalued at the time of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's recent massive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to lower the value of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I don't want to make any comment" about the prudence of Japan's market move, said Haruhiko Kuroda, president of the Asian Development Bank. The former vice-minister for international affairs and top spokesman on Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  issues from 1999 to 2003 nevertheless said the yen, at the time the government moved in, "was not reflecting fundamentals" and it appeared overvalued, given the relative weakness of Japan compared to other major nations.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "It is always difficult" to determine what is happening in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets, and what can be accomplished by governments when they try to affect \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  values via \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Kuroda said. That said, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  "should reflect fundamentals" and the rising value of the yen wasn't doing that over the short and medium term, given the "weak" recovery seen in Japan, he said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Kuroda declined to comment on the specifics of what would constitute an appropriate exchange rate for the yen relative to other major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . He also declined, in an interview in New York with Dow Jones Newswires, to predict the future path of his nation's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's financial authorities \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets last Wednesday in a bid to weaken Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  relative to the nation's major trading partners. The Y2 trillion \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was the first by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in six years, and it may have been the largest such single-day action in history. The dollar jumped about three yen higher on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and has traded above Y85 since then.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In other comments, Kuroda said he doesn't believe Japan, Europe or the U.S. will slip back into recession. Asian-area growth is by and large turning out to be stronger than expected, and forecasts for that area produced by the Asian Development Bank may see modest upward revisions, he said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Speaking before the outcome of the Federal Reserve policy meeting, he said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had been doing an "excellent job" in supporting the U.S. economy, although he declined to speculate on whether the institution would take additional steps to support the economy. He also said the Fed will do what it takes to make sure deflation doesn't take hold in the U.S. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    -By Michael S. Derby, Dow Jones Newswires, 212-416-2214;   michael.derby@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 September 21, 2010 13:33 ET (17:33 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020100921e69l004cb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
